From c566162ca889405c3c04d2fab2e35d0209567e46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elmo Todurov <elmo_git@todurov.eu>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 06:49:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 96/97] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: tune battery data

Replace the rounded placeholder battery values with figures from
the Xiaomi downstream battery profile, and add the two properties
the simple-battery binding lets us populate but were previously
omitted:

  charge-full-design-microamp-hours: 5150 -> 5160 mAh
  constant-charge-current-max-microamp:    (new) 2 A
  energy-full-design-microwatt-hours:      (new) 19.866 Wh

Capacity (5160 mAh) is taken from Xiaomi's vayu battery profile
DTSI: qcom,nom-batt-capacity-mah = <5160>.

energy-full-design (19 866 000 uWh) is computed as
5160 mAh x 3.85 V (standard Li-ion nominal); downstream's battery
profile does not state a separate nominal voltage.

constant-charge-current-max-microamp is set to a conservative 2 A.
Downstream advertises qcom,fastchg-current-ma = <5900> (5.9 A), but
that ceiling is gated by Xiaomi-specific battery authentication,
thermal throttling and charge-pump sequencing that mainline does
not implement. 2 A is well within what PM8150B can deliver safely
without any of that policy.

voltage-max-design-microvolt is left at 4.4 V rather than the
downstream 4.475 V to limit cell heating; the extra 75 mV
downstream is paired with thermal management not yet present in
mainline. The downstream value is recorded as a comment for
future reference.

Source:
https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource (vayu-r-oss)
  arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/fg-gen4-batterydata-vayu-NVT-5160mah.dtsi
  arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/fg-gen4-batterydata-vayu-sunwoda-5160mah.dtsi

Signed-off-by: Elmo Todurov <elmo_git@todurov.eu>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi   | 21 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
index ee0f877a6e..d6ad8ac715 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
@@ -53,8 +53,27 @@ aliases {
 
 	battery: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
-		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5150000>;
+		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5160000>;
+		/*
+		 * Energy = 5160 mAh * 3.85 V (standard Li-ion nominal);
+		 * downstream profile does not state a nominal voltage.
+		 */
+		energy-full-design-microwatt-hours = <19866000>;
+		/*
+		 * Downstream advertises qcom,fastchg-current-ma = <5900>,
+		 * but that ceiling is gated by Xiaomi-specific battery
+		 * authentication, thermal throttling and charge-pump
+		 * sequencing not implemented in mainline. 2 A is well
+		 * within what PM8150B can deliver safely without that.
+		 */
+		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <2000000>;
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
+		/*
+		 * Downstream qcom,max-voltage-uv = <4475000> (4.475 V).
+		 * Held at 4.4 V here to limit cell heating; the extra
+		 * 75 mV downstream is paired with thermal management
+		 * that mainline does not yet have.
+		 */
 		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4400000>;
 	};
 
